        "math_academy_id": "q-73024",
        "problem": "Given that $k\\ge 0$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(k+1)!}{k!}.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(k+1)!=(k+1)\\cdot k!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $k!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(k+1)!}{k!} & =\\frac{(k+1)\\cdot k!}{k!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k+1)\\cdot \\cancel{k!}}{\\cancel{k!}} \\\\  & =k+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
